  { q: "Can Wafeq handle credit notes for returns?", a: "You must issue an e-credit note linked to the original invoice when you correct a sent invoice. Create it in Wafeq and send a test credit note before you go live. Each credit note counts as one document." },
  { q: "Can I edit a Wafeq invoice after I send it as an e-invoice?", a: "No. Once an e-invoice is sent, you cannot edit it. You issue a credit note to correct it. Then you send a new e-invoice if the sale must be billed again." },
  { q: "Do walk-in retail sales need e-invoices?", a: "Not for now. Sales to consumers (B2C) are outside the system. But a walk-in buyer who gives you a company TRN is a B2B customer. That sale needs an e-invoice once your phase starts." },
  { q: "How does a contractor bill retention in Wafeq?", a: "Keep retention outside the invoice total. The progress e-invoice may cover the net certified amount. When the retention is released, you issue a separate e-invoice for it. Confirm the treatment with your tax adviser." },
  { q: "Is Wafeq good for distributors with many invoices?", a: "It can be. Wafeq says its accounting product suits businesses that send fewer than 500 invoices a month. Above that, or with a large ERP, ask Wafeq whether your plan fits." },
  { q: "Can I move my data from QuickBooks or Excel to Wafeq?", a: "Yes. We move your data and quote the price on WhatsApp, because it depends on your data. See our switching page." },
  { q: "What if I already use another ASP?", a: "You can switch to Wafeq. Offboard your current ASP on EmaraTax, then appoint Wafeq right after." },
  { q: "When is the e-invoicing deadline for Wafeq users?", a: "It is the same as for every business. With revenue under AED 50 million, appoint an ASP by 31 March 2027 and go live on 1 July 2027. With revenue of AED 50 million or more, the appointment date was 30 October 2026 and go-live is 1 January 2027. Government entities go live on 1 October 2027." },
  { q: "What is the penalty for missing the e-invoicing deadline?", a: "Not appointing an ASP on time costs AED 5,000 for each month. After go-live, each invoice not issued electronically can cost AED 100, up to AED 5,000 a month. Credit notes have the same rule." },
  { q: "Can einvoicecost.ae set up Wafeq e-invoicing for me?", a: `Yes. We do the full setup for ${aed(P.help)}, one time. It covers data fixes, your EmaraTax appointment, a test invoice and credit note, and fixes for rejected invoices. Or set it up yourself for free with the steps in this guide.` },
];

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: 'https://einvoicecost.ae/' },
  { name: 'Blog', url: 'https://einvoicecost.ae/blog' },
  { name: 'Wafeq e-invoicing UAE', url: URL },
];

const article = {
