    <section id="mistakes">
      <h2>Mistakes that cause rejected e-invoices</h2>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>Missing customer TRNs.</b> This is the most common problem. Fix the gaps first.</li>
        <li><b>Names that do not match.</b> The customer's legal name must match its registration. A trading name will not do. Check your own name too.</li>
        <li><b>Items with no VAT treatment.</b> Every item needs the right treatment. Check each one.</li>
        <li><b>Discounts with no reason.</b> A discount or charge that changes the invoice value should be clear and explained.</li>
        <li><b>Editing after sending.</b> You cannot. Credit notes fix mistakes. Check every invoice before you send it.</li>
        <li><b>Mixing B2B and B2C.</b> Do not skip a business customer. And do not treat a consumer receipt as an e-invoice. Mark customer types clearly.</li>
        <li><b>Letting your plan lapse.</b> If your subscription ends, your e-invoicing may stop. Renew before the date.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="know">
      <h2>Things to know before you start</h2>
      <ul class="know">
        <li><b>A PDF is not an e-invoice.</b> Emailing a PDF will not count for invoices in scope. The legal invoice is the structured one that goes through your ASP. You can still send a PDF as a courtesy copy.</li>
        <li><b>You appoint one ASP.</b> The same ASP handles the e-invoices you send and the ones you receive.</li>
        <li><b>Already have another ASP?</b> You can move to Wafeq. Wafeq says you offboard your current ASP on EmaraTax, then appoint Wafeq straight after. Your current ASP must release you right away.</li>
        <li><b>Keep your records.</b> Plan to keep e-invoices and credit notes for five years. Ask Wafeq what storage your plan includes and how you can export your documents.</li>
        <li><b>Check the latest plan details.</b> Wafeq says e-invoicing is part of the plan, but it does not state every plan limit in one place. Read the plan page before you pay.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="switch">
      <h2>Using QuickBooks or Excel today? Think about switching</h2>
      <p>Some businesses read this guide and ask a fair question: "Should I move to Wafeq?" It depends. If your accounting software already works for you, staying is fine. QuickBooks and Excel users can stay and add an outside ASP. We set that up. See our <a href="/quickbooks-online">QuickBooks Online</a> and <a href="/excel">Excel</a> pages for exact prices.</p>
      <p>But if you are unhappy with your software, or the e-invoicing cost bothers you, moving to Wafeq is an option. Wafeq, Zoho Books and TallyPrime all have e-invoicing built in. We move your data from QuickBooks or Excel into Wafeq. The price depends on how much data you have, so we quote it on WhatsApp. Read <a href="/switch-accounting-software">how switching works</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="help">
      <h2>Set it up yourself, or get help?</h2>
      <p>You can set up Wafeq yourself for free. The five steps above are enough for many businesses. If your customer and item data are clean, you may finish in an afternoon. Get help in three cases: your data is messy, you have many customers or items, or you have no time to test.</p>
      <p>Our setup costs {aed(P.help)}, one time. We check your plan against your invoice count. We check and fix your customer TRNs, VAT codes and items. We handle your registration and EmaraTax appointment. We send a test invoice and a test credit note. We fix any rejected invoice. And we show your staff how it works.</p>
      <p>Not on Wafeq? Other software has its own path. Zoho Books and TallyPrime also have e-invoicing built in. See our guides to <a href="/blog/zoho-e-invoicing-uae-guide">Zoho Books</a> and <a href="/blog/tally-e-invoicing-uae-guide">Tally</a>, or the page for <a href="/other-software">other software</a>.</p>
      <p class="callout">Want help with your own Wafeq setup? Message us on <a href={`https://wa.me/${WA}`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">WhatsApp</a>, or use the <a href="/">einvoicecost.ae price calculator →</a></p>
    </section>

